  "notes": "{拭|ふ}く is a transitive verb (⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧) for wiping surfaces clean or dry.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{拭|ふ}いている indicates wiping is in progress.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [surface]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}く — to wipe [surface]\n- [moisture/dirt]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}く — to wipe away [moisture/dirt]\n- [cloth]⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{拭|ふ}く — to wipe with [cloth]\n- ⟦{汗|あせ}→汗：02173_ase⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}く (wipe sweat)\n- ⟦{涙|なみだ}→涙：02235_namida⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}く (wipe tears)\n- ⟦{床|ゆか}→床：03652_yuka⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}く (wipe/mop the floor)\n- ⟦{拭|ふ}き{掃除|そうじ}→拭き掃除：18123_fukisouji⟧ (wiping/mopping)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {拭|ふ}く (to wipe) — different from:\n- ⟦{吹|ふ}く→吹く：02445_fuku⟧ (to blow)\n- ⟦{噴|ふ}く→噴く：26557_fuku⟧ (to spout)\n\nAll three can be read ふく but have different meanings.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{雑巾|ぞうきん}→雑巾：04408_zoukin⟧ (cleaning rag)\n- ⟦{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る→拭き取る：18690_fukitoru⟧ (to wipe off)",
